From 679ae09532c916284db417553fe44026331db124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:47:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): pool wait notices count what matching workers
 claim first [daveey]

Machine-lane wait notices and `kanban show` queue notes printed
`kanban_label_backlog.words()`, whose `ahead` counts only ready predecessors whose
`runs_on` EQUALS the card's labels. Predecessors with other label sets that the same
workers claim first (e.g. `["pool:worker"]`) were not counted, so a card deep in the
pool queue read "0 card(s) with matching labels ahead of it" and owner chats chased a
dispatch bug that did not exist (t_d943a79dd2b3889f: notice said 0 ahead; queue
--explain put it 13/31; 33 pool-eligible ready cards outscored it and the next three
claims were exactly the top three of those; 47 of 224 matching_pool_busy notices in
24 h carried the "0 ... ahead" text).

Change:
- `read()` takes optional `machine_labels` (matching machine -> effective labels).
  When given, the result carries `pool_ahead`: ready, unclaimed predecessors in
  `lane_rows` order with a non-empty label set that one of those machines carries.
  Computed in the existing loop over the ready-row SELECT (no new query). Label-less
  predecessors are not counted (approximate, documented). Without it, no key.
- `placement()` passes `machine_labels` for the available matching machines from the
  `carried` map it already builds. Attach condition unchanged; `backlog=False`
  dispatch path untouched (737b7f30765).
- `words()` prepends "N ready card(s) ahead that its matching workers can also run; "
  only when `pool_ahead` is present; the rest stays byte-identical. `move_refusal()`
  still calls `read()` without it, so its text is unchanged.

Proof:
- New tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_label_backlog_pool_ahead.py: (a)-(d) fail before
  (TypeError on machine_labels / KeyError pool_ahead), pass after; (e) no-key
  regression passes before and after.
- Guards unchanged and green: test_kanban_label_backlog_wait.py (43),
  test_kanban_dispatch_placement_backlog.py (3), test_kanban_notice_pacing_admission.py
  (65). 36 test files importing the touched modules: 900 passed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.

